Quantity : 2000', NULL, NULL, '• Complete audited balance sheets and profit and loss account for the immediate three preceding financial years.
• Certificate from a Practicing Chartered Accountant towards the turnover of the Bidder along with copy of its Income Tax Return (not acknowledgement) - if not required to get accounts audited under Section 44AD of The Income Tax Act, 1961.
• Consolidated audited annual report - if a Parent Company has wholly owned subsidiaries and only a single consolidated report is prepared and audited, with a certification from the statutory auditor.
• Consolidated audited annual report - if a subsidiary company''s separate annual report is not prepared and audited, with a certification from the parent company''s statutory auditor.
• Financial details of the three previous years - if the financial year closing date is within 6 months of the original bid due date and the audited annual report of the immediately preceding financial year is not available.
• Letter from CA stating reasons for non-preparation/furnishing of the latest year’s Audited Financial Statements - if the financial year closing date is within 6-9 months of the original bid due date and the audited annual report of the immediately preceding financial year is not available.
• Financial details of the immediate three preceding financial years - if the financial year closing date is beyond 9 months of the original bid due date.
• Audited Financial Report in a currency other than INR, with conversion factor indicated in the report or RBI Reference Rate.
• Certificate/reports issued/attested by a practicing chartered accountant in India, including stamp, signature, and UDIN number.
• Work order(s)/ Purchase order(s) (PO)/ Letter of Acceptance (LoA) indicating the similar work.
• Invoice / Completion Certificate/s issued / Delivery Receipts / Client Acknowledgements / Payment Receipts / Client Endorsement by mail or letters/ acknowledged final report or any other document to support successful completion of similar works.
• Completion certificate issued by the main contractor to the subcontractor, along with client approval/acknowledgement for engaging the bidder as a subcontractor - if jobs are subcontracted.
• Proof of payment like bills/invoices, payment receipt, bank statement/GST receipt etc. - for subcontracted jobs, establishing payment made against the PO/WO/Contract.
• Tender Specific Requirement documents.
• Credentials submitted in support of PQC, in the name of the entity bidding for the tender.
• Attested copy of the legal agreement for JV - if the bidder has completed similar nature of work as a JV.
• Form – X detailing PO / Work Order, Completion Certificates, and client contact information.
• Self-certified documents in original from CEO or CFO or Company Secretary of the bidder (Limited company only) - as an alternative to certification by Statutory Auditors or Practicing Chartered Accountant.
• CEO / CFO''s certificate in original - if the bidding entity is unable to submit an audited balance sheet due to internal/local regulations, stating turnover and net worth, with a declaration and endorsement by a Chartered Accountant / Statutory Auditor / Certified Public Accountant.
• CEO / CFO''s certificate in original without endorsement - if Chartered Accountant / Statutory Auditor / Certified Public Accountant cannot provide endorsement due to local regulations, with a reference to the local regulation.
• Udyam Certificate (for MSE eligibility).
• Vendor declaration regarding status of debarment/holiday listing by other PSUs/GeM.
