st layer, 2nd layer, 3rd layer, 4th Layer)67. Maximum permissible conductor temperature for continuous operation68. Maximum permissible conductor temperature for short term operation69. Permissible duration of above short term operation70. Steady state conductor temperatute at conductor current of minimum 640A at 50°C ambient conditions & zero wind71. DC resistance of conductor at 20°C72. AC resistance at maximum continuous operating temperature corresponding to specified maximum operating current73. Details of Creep characteristic for conductor enclosed74. Sag Tension Calculation enclosed75. Sag & Tension at 30°C & no wind76. Sag & Tension at 30°C & full wind77. Sag & Tension at 50°C & 2/3rd wind78. Sag & Tension at 60°C & no wind79. Sag & Tension at 150°C & no wind80. Sag & Tension at maximum operating temperature & no wind81. Sag & Tension at emergency temperature & no wind82. Tolerance on standard length of conductor83. Direction of lay for outside layer84. Linear mass of the conductor (Standard, Minimum, Maximum)85. Standard length of conductor86. Maximum length of conductor that can be offered as single length87. Drum is as per specification88. Accessories is as per specification/standards89. Certificates of completed work orders from clients preferably State Electricity Board regarding the last three year''s orders received/executed.90. Details of insurance coverage91. Copy of Contract Labour Regulation Abolition Act92. Copy of Workmen’s Compensation Act93. Copy of Minimum Wages Act94. Copy of Payment of Wages Act', '2026-07-13 07:02:02.786', '2026-07-13 07:02:02.786', NULL, NULL, 'cable,conductors,date', NULL, '91466463', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '100396645', 'NOT_DECIDED', 'NOT_DECIDED', 'NOT_DECIDED', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
