subcontracted12. Form of Undertaking on Compliance of Terms & Conditions of the RFB/ bidding document including Scope of Work and other related requirements13. Statement of Deviation from the requirements specified in the RFB/ bidding documents including Conditions of Contract, Employer’s Requirement/ Specification and Drawings etc14. Work Completion Schedule15. Guarantee Declaration16. Information regarding ex-employees of Employer in our firm17. Filled up information regarding Price Adjustment Data18. Option for Interest bearing Initial Advance payment and Information for E-payment, PF details and declaration regarding Micro/Small & Medium Enterprises19. Declaration for tax exemptions, reductions, allowances or benefits20. Bank Guarantee verification checklist21. Additional Information, if any22. Integrity Pact, duly signed on each page by the person signing the bid23. Self-certified copy of the document to establish legal status of the firm viz. Certificate of Incorporation issued under The Companies Act / The Limited Liability Partnership Act / Partnership deed etc. as applicable24. Self-certified copy of PAN25. Self-certified copy of GST Registration26. Self-certified copy in support of MSME, if applicable27. Certificate from banker indicating various fund based/non fund based limits sanctioned to the bidder and the extent of utilization as on date.28. Complete annual reports together with Audited statement of accounts of the company for last five years of its own (separate) immediately preceding the date of submission of bid.29. Audited balance sheets, income statements, other information pertaining to its own (not of its group/Holding/Parent Company) duly certified by any one of the authority [(i) Statutory Auditor of the bidder /(ii) Company Secretary of the bidder or (iii) A certified Public Accountant] certifying that such information/documents are based on the audited accounts as the case may be.30. Certificate from banker indicating various fund based/non fund based limits sanctioned to the bidder or each member of the joint venture and the extent of utilization as on date.31. Details of Banker32. Current Contract Commitments of works in progress33. Financial Data34. CV and experience details of a project manager with 15 years’ experience in executing such contract of comparable nature including not less than five years as manager and the CVs of other employees to be deputed for the subject work35. Safety Plan (Annexure – 1A (SP))36. Manpower deployment plan (Annexure – 1B (SP))37. List of Lifting Machines i.e. Crane, Hoist, Triffor, Chain Pulley Blocks etc. and Lifting Tools and Tackles i.e. D shackle, Pulleys, come along clamps, wire rope slings etc. and all types of ropes i.e. Wire ropes, Poly propylene Rope etc. used for lifting purposes along with test certificates. (Annexure – 2 (SP))38. List of Personal Protective Equipment (PPE), activity wise including the following along with test certificate of each as applicable.39. Industrial Safety Helmet to all workmen at site. (EN 397 / IS 2925) with chin strap and back stay arrangement.40. Safety shoes without steel toe to all ground level workers and canvas shoes for workers working on tower.41. Rubber Gum Boot to workers working in rainy season / concreting job.42. Twin lanyard Full Body Safety harness with shock absorber and leg strap arrangement for all workers working at height for more than three meters. Safety Harness should be with attachments of light weight such as of aluminum alloy etc. and having a feature of automatic locking arrangement of snap hook and comply with EN 361 / IS 3521 standards.43. Mobile fall arrestors for safety of workers during their ascending / descending from tower / on tower. EN 353 -2 (Guided type fall arresters on a flexible anchorage line.)44. Retractable type fall arrestor (EN360: 2002) for ascending / descending on suspension insulator string etc.45. Providing of good quality cotton hand gloves / leather hand gloves for workers engaged in handling of tower parts or as per requirement at site.46. Electrical Resistance hand gloves to workers for handling electrical equipment / Electrical connections. IS : 477047. Dust masks to workers handling cement as per requirement.48. Face shield for welder and Grinders. IS : 1179 / IS : 255349. Other PPEs, if any, as per requirement etc.50. List of Earthing Equipment / Earthing devices with Earthing lead conforming to IECs for earthing equipment are – (855, 1230, 1235 etc.) gang wise for stringing activity/as per requirement. (Annexure – 4 (SP))51. List of Qualified Safety Officer(s) along with their contact details (Annexure – 5A (SP))52. Details of Explosive Operator (if required), Safety officer / Safety supervisor for every erection / stinging gang, any other person nominated for safety, list of personnel trained in First Aid as well as brief information about safety set up by the Contractor along with copy of organisation of the Contractor in regard to safety. (Annexure – 5B (SP))53. Copy of Safety Policy/ Safety Document of the Contractor’s company (Annexure – 6 (SP))54. Emergency Preparedness Plan’ for different incidences i.e. Fall from height, Electrocution, Sun Stroke, Collapse of pit, Collapse of Tower, Snake bite, Fire in camp / Store, Flood, Storm, Earthquake, Militancy etc. while carrying out different activities under execution i.e. foundation works including civil works, erection, stringing (as applicable), testing & commissioning, disposal of materials at site / store etc. (Annexure – 7 (SP))55. Safety Audit Check Lists (Annexure – 8 (SP))56. Copy of the module of Safety Training Programs on Safety, Health and Environment, safe execution of different activities of works for Contractor’s own employees on regular basis and sub-Contractor employees. (Annexure – 9 (SP))57. Information along with documentary evidences in regard to the Contractor’s compliance to various statutory requirements including the following:58. Electricity Act 200359. Factories Act 1948 or latest60. Building & other construction workers (Regulation of Employment and Conditions of Services Act and Central Act 1996 or latest) and Welfare Cess Act 1996 or latest with Rules.61. Workmen Compensation Act 1923 or latest and Rules.62. Public Insurance Liabilities Act 1991 or latest and Rules.63. Indian Explosive Act 1948 or latest and Rules.64. Indian Petroleum Act 1934 or latest and Rules.65. License under the contract Labour (Regulation & Abolition) Act 1970 or latest and Rules.66. Indian Electricity Rule 2003 and amendments if any, from time to time.67. The Environment (Protection) Act 1986 or latest and Rules.68. Child Labour (Prohibition & Regulation) Act 1986 or latest.69. National Building Code of India 2005 or latest (NBC 2005).70. Indian standards for construction of Low/ Medium/ High/ Extra High Voltage Transmission Line71. Any other statutory requirement(s) [please specify]72. Details of Insurance Policies along with documentary evidences taken by the Contractor for the insurance coverage against accident for all employees as below:73. Workmen Compensation Act 1923 or latest and Rules.74. Public Insurance Liabilities Act 1991 or latest75. Any Other Insurance Policies76. Joint Deed of Undertaking by the Joint Venture Partners/ Members77. Format for evidence of access to or availability of credit/facilities (Bank Certificate)78. Format of Operational Acceptance79. Format of Safety Plan to be Submitted by the Contractor Within Sixty Days of Award of Contract80. List of approved Subcontractors81. Scope of Works and Supply by the Employer82. List of Documents for Approval or Review83. Guarantees, Liquidated Damages for Non-Performance84. Performance Security Form85. Bank Guarantee Form for Advance Payment86. Form of Indemnity Bond to be Executed by the Contractor for the Equipment Handed Over in One Lot87. Form of Indemnity Bond to be Executed by the Contractor for the Equipment Handed Over in Installments88. Form of Authorization Letter89. Form of Trust Receipt for Plant, Equipment and Materials Received90. Form of Extension of Bank Guarantee91. Form of Power of Attorney for Joint Venture92. Form of Joint Deed of Undertaking by the Sub-Contractor Alongwith the Contractor93. Form of Certificate of Financial Parameters for QR', '2026-07-13 07:02:11.599', '2026-07-13 07:24:21.629', 'The tender brief is for a turnkey contract that includes installation and commissioning, without explicitly stating the supply of eligible products.', false, 'cable,conductors', NULL, '1689378685', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '101684890', 'NOT_DECIDED', 'NOT_DECIDED', 'NOT_DECIDED', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
